       }
     ]
   }
 ]
}

But need to ensure each reaction's children are molecules (no further nesting). The precursor molecules for each reaction are as given in apply_template outputs.

We need to map which precursor corresponds to which reaction:

- For 29646: precursor list from apply_template-1: only one precursor: "C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](C/C=C/C=C/C(=O)O[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)C[C@H](O)[C@H]1C)CO"

- For 1914389: apply_template-2 gave two precursors: 
   1) "C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](CC=O)C[C@H](O[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)[C@H]1C)CO"
   2) "CCOC(=O)/C=C/CP(=O)(OCC)OCC"

- For 1914390: apply_template-3 gave one precursor: "CCOC(=O)C[C@H]1C[C@H](O[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](/C=C(/C)C(=O)OC)O1"

- For 149040: apply_template-4 gave two precursors: "CC(C)(C)[Si](C)(C)OS(=O)(=O)C(F)(F)F" and "CCOC(=O)C[C@H]1C[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](/C=C(/C)C(=O)OC)O1"

- For 1914391: apply_template-5 gave two precursors: "CCOC(=O)C[C@H]1C[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](C=O)O1" and "COC#CC(C)P(=O)(OCC(F)(F)F)OCC(F)(F)F"

Now we need to embed these correctly. The precursor for 1914389 should be the same molecule as the product of 29646? Actually the product of 29646 is the TBS protected molecule (precursor1). That same molecule is also the substrate for 1914389? The apply_template-2 used the same target molecule (the original target?) Wait the target for template 1914389 is the same final molecule? The input says "apply the template as the result of the task make_5_lvl2-template_search-2 to the molecule below". The molecule below likely is the same final molecule. So the precursor list from 1914389 are alternative disconnections, not necessarily sequential. But we can still embed them as separate branches from the same molecule node (precursor1). That's okay.

Thus we can have precursor1 node with multiple reaction children (each representing a different retrosynthetic step). That's allowed.

